<title>USA: IMF approves $75 mln loan for Macedonia.</title>
<headline>IMF approves $75 mln loan for Macedonia.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Monetary Fund Friday aproved a $75 million, three-year loan for Macedonia to supoort its 1997-99 economic reform program.</p>
<p>The IMF, in a written statement, noted that despite gains made through an economic program launched in 1994, Macedonia's economy &quot;has yet to turn around decisively.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;The unemployment rate is as high as 30 per cent and the banking system is suffering from low collection rates and wide interest rates spreads,&quot; the IMF said.</p>
</text>
